    coverageRequired: "Nevada requires employers to secure workers' compensation coverage for their employees; there is effectively no minimum-employee-count exemption for a true employer with employees (Nevada Industrial Insurance Act, NRS Chapters 616A–616D). The notable carve-outs are for the business owner's own coverage (sole proprietor, partner, LLC member) and for corporate officers/LLC managers, both described below.",
