    corporateOfficers: "Officers or managers of a quasi-public or private corporation (and LLC managers) are automatically included in workers' compensation coverage requirements by default. They may REJECT coverage for themselves under NRS 616B.624 by filing a written rejection with the company and its insurer; the rejection can later be rescinded in writing. Multiple secondary sources (insurance-industry pages, not an .nv.gov page I could render as text) identify the specific form used for this rejection as Nevada Division of Industrial Relations Form D-43 ('Employee Election to Reject Coverage and Election to Waive the Rejection of Coverage for Excluded Persons'). I was unable to directly render the official dir.nv.gov PDF (it returned as an image-based/encoded PDF I could not extract text from, and a second larger training PDF was also not machine-readable via the fetch tool), so the D-43 form name/number is corroborated only by secondary sources and should be verified against a live dir.nv.gov copy before publishing the specific form number as fact. No numeric cap on the number of officers who may reject coverage was found.",
