    howToFile: "A business entity with no employees other than the owner(s)/partner(s)/officer(s)/director(s) it wants excluded applies to the Utah Labor Commission for a Workers' Compensation Coverage Waiver (WCCW), online at webaccess.laborcommission.utah.gov/wccoveragewaivers/. Applicant must submit supporting documentation under Utah Code § 34A-2-1004 (two or more of: prior-year tax return showing business income, a valid business license, an occupational/professional license, or proof of active liability insurance; or one of those plus two of: bank account proof, phone number + physical location proof, or an advertisement showing the business name/contact info) and pay a fee set by the Commission not to exceed $50 (§ 34A-2-1003(1)(d)). The waiver expires one year from issuance and must be renewed (same fee cap, same information) to stay in effect; it becomes invalid the moment the business employs anyone beyond the named owner(s)/officer(s)/director(s).",
